### 23\. Audit and outstanding blockers

| Audit category | Finding                                                                                                  |
| -------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Summary        | Six donor platforms mapped to a unified UAP architecture                                                 |
| Threat model   | Cross-tenant access, excessive privileges, credential leakage, dependency risks and unauthorized actions |
| Tests          | Acceptance requirements defined; no new implementation tests executed                                    |
| Invariants     | Stable SID, Hermes reasoning authority, unified policy, existing ecosystem preservation                  |
| Diacritics     | Existing canonical ecosystem names preserved                                                             |

Outstanding blockers and decisions:

* The Nightly OpenBot and CopilotKit OpenBot repositories were reviewed through their public documentation, but their complete local source trees were not inspected.

* Nightly and DuskBot require commercial authorization for reuse of their current restricted code.

* UAP's development and deployment commits differ.

* Existing UAP documentation identifies its deployed foundation as single-owner rather than a fully isolated commercial SaaS platform.

* The existing 235-item checklist has not yet been reconciled item by item with this supplemental checklist.

* The proposed palette, avatar behavior, repository structure and quality scoring system are design decisions made for this blueprint; they are not existing production features.

No repositories were cloned during this planning pass, and no files, services or production applications were modified.

The next implementation step is to establish a verified donor-source registry, freeze the existing UAP foundation, and begin the original Nightly-inspired workspace and plush companion redesign on an isolated development branch.
